The programme, organised under the Arts & Music Envoy Program of the US Department of State's Bureau of Educational and Cultural Affairs, will include mentorship, interactive sessions and collaboration with Nepali singers, musicians, songwriters, producers, artist managers and other music professionals.

The sessions will focus on songwriting, music business, digital platforms, copyright and the wider music industry, according to the US Embassy.

