US Chargé d'Affaires Scott Urbom said the programme would help strengthen professional connections between American and Nepali artists while supporting creativity and growth in Nepal's music sector.

The programme will conclude with a public concert at The Plaza, Pulchowk, on August 29. The concert will feature performances by Lynn, Nepali artists Rato Rani and Ujan Shakya, and a fusion performance by Lynn and sarangi player Kiran Nepali, a US government exchange programme alumnus.
